@page "/guide"

<PageTitle>Guide · Ardán</PageTitle>

<PageHeader Title="Guide" Subtitle="What you are looking at, what each part does and how to work with it. About five minutes from start to finish.">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="live"><Icon Name="live" Size="16" />Open the live view</a>
</PageHeader>

<div class="guide">
    <nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <span class="guide-toc-title">On this page</span>
        @foreach (var (id, title) in Sections)
        {
            <a href="@($"guide#{id}")">@title</a>
        }
    </nav>

    <div class="guide-body">
        <section id="start" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Start here</h2>
            <p class="guide-lead">
                Ardán runs an automated, chilled pallet store. Pallets arrive from suppliers, are stored in a six-level rack and leave
                for the docks when an order needs them. Machines do the moving; you watch, decide and step in when something needs a person.
            </p>
            <ol class="guide-steps">
                <li>
                    <span class="guide-step">1</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Look at the store</strong>
                        <p>Overview sums up the shift. The live view shows every machine moving in 3D.</p>
                        <a class="link" href="live">Open the live view <Icon Name="chevron-right" Size="14" /></a>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="guide-step">2</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Click anything</strong>
                        <p>A Taxi, a VTU, a conveyor or a lane opens on the right with what it is doing and what you can do.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="guide-step">3</span>
                    <div>
                        <strong>Fix what turns red</strong>
                        <p>A red ! marks a stop. The alert at the bottom right has the fix button; Alarms has every step.</p>
                        <a class="link" href="alarms">Open Alarms <Icon Name="chevron-right" Size="14" /></a>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="hint">This is a demo with made-up data. Everyone who opens it shares the same store, so every button is safe to try.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="store" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>The store and its machines</h2>
            <div class="guide-grid">
                @foreach (var part in Parts)
                {
                    <article class="guide-part">
                        <span class="guide-part-icon tone-@part.Tone"><Icon Name="@part.Icon" Size="20" /></span>
                        <strong>@part.Name</strong>
                        <p>@part.Text</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="flow" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>How a pallet moves</h2>
            <h3 class="guide-flow-title"><i class="swatch flow-in"></i>Into store</h3>
            <div class="flow guide-flow">
                @for (var i = 0; i < Inbound.Length; i++)
                {
                    if (i > 0)
                    {
                        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><Icon Name="arrow-right" /></span>
                    }
                    <div class="flow-node"><Icon Name="@Inbound[i].Icon" /><strong>@Inbound[i].Name</strong><span>@Inbound[i].Text</span></div>
                }
            </div>
            <h3 class="guide-flow-title"><i class="swatch flow-out"></i>Out of store</h3>
            <div class="flow guide-flow">
                @for (var i = 0; i < Outbound.Length; i++)
                {
                    if (i > 0)
                    {
                        <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><Icon Name="arrow-right" /></span>
                    }
                    <div class="flow-node"><Icon Name="@Outbound[i].Icon" /><strong>@Outbound[i].Name</strong><span>@Outbound[i].Text</span></div>
                }
            </div>
            <p class="hint">One Taxi works an aisle at a time. A Taxi that needs another level waits at the dock for the first free VTU.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="live" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Reading the live view</h2>
            <div class="guide-split">
                <div>
                    <h3>In the 3D store</h3>
                    <dl class="guide-legend">
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-tag is-in">T-01 ↓ L1·B04</span></dt><dd>Taxi T-01 is taking a pallet into store. It is heading for level 1, bay 4.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-tag is-out">T-03 ↑ Outfeed</span></dt><dd>Taxi T-03 is taking a pallet out of store, to the outfeed and the docks.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-tag">T-05 ⚡</span></dt><dd>Charging at the dock. A label with just the name means the Taxi is free.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-alert">!</span></dt><dd>A machine has stopped or needs a decision. Point at it to see why; click it for the steps.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-arrows"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></dt><dd>Moving arrows show a Taxi's route. A frame marks the lane or conveyor it is going to.</dd></div>
                        <div><dt><span class="guide-pallets"><i class="is-plain"></i><i class="is-amber"></i></span></dt><dd>Pallets in their lanes. Amber means best before within three days. The layers button colours lanes by speed or expiry instead.</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Around it</h3>
                    <dl class="guide-legend">
                        @foreach (var (name, text) in Panels)
                        {
                            <div><dt><span class="guide-place">@name</span></dt><dd>@text</dd></div>
                        }
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="controls" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Controls</h2>
            <div class="guide-split">
                <div>
                    <h3><Icon Name="mouse" Size="16" />Mouse and touch</h3>
                    <dl class="guide-keys">
                        @foreach (var (key, text) in Pointer)
                        {
                            <div><dt>@key</dt><dd>@text</dd></div>
                        }
                    </dl>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3><Icon Name="keyboard" Size="16" />Keyboard</h3>
                    <dl class="guide-keys">
                        @foreach (var (keys, text) in Keys)
                        {
                            <div>
                                <dt>
                                    @foreach (var key in keys)
                                    {
                                        <kbd>@key</kbd>
                                    }
                                </dt>
                                <dd>@text</dd>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="hint">The camera keeps a fixed angle so the store never turns upside down. Lock it before a demo and the mouse can only click.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="actions" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Taking action</h2>
            <p>Every action asks for confirmation and says what will happen before anything moves.</p>
            <div class="guide-grid">
                @foreach (var action in Actions)
                {
                    <article class="guide-part">
                        <span class="guide-part-icon tone-@action.Tone"><Icon Name="@action.Icon" Size="20" /></span>
                        <strong>@action.Name</strong>
                        <p>@action.Text</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="score" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>The shift score</h2>
            <p>
                A light layer of game on top of real work: points for what the shift gets done, stars for keeping customers' orders on time
                and goals to aim for. It only watches. Nothing about the score changes how the store runs.
            </p>
            <div class="guide-split">
                <dl class="guide-points">
                    @foreach (var (what, points) in Points)
                    {
                        <div><dt>@what</dt><dd class="@(points.StartsWith('−') ? "is-loss" : "is-gain")">@points</dd></div>
                    }
                </dl>
                <dl class="guide-legend">
                    <div><dt><span class="guide-place">Stars</span></dt><dd>How many of the last 20 orders finished on time, from 0 to 5 in half stars.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt><span class="guide-place">Goals</span></dt><dd>Store, send, finish on time, fix stops, run without a stop. Each pays its reward and comes back a little harder.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt><span class="guide-place">Suggestions</span></dt><dd>Work worth doing now, such as rushing an order that is nearly due. Nothing changes until you accept one.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="pages" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Every page</h2>
            <div class="guide-pages">
                @foreach (var link in Pages)
                {
                    <a class="guide-page" href="@link.Href">
                        <span class="guide-part-icon tone-brand"><Icon Name="@link.Icon" Size="18" /></span>
                        <span><strong>@link.Name</strong><small>@link.Text</small></span>
                        <Icon Name="chevron-right" Size="16" Class="guide-go" />
                    </a>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="words" class="card guide-section">
            <h2>Words used here</h2>
            <dl class="guide-words">
                @foreach (var (word, meaning) in Words)
                {
                    <div><dt>@word</dt><dd>@meaning</dd></div>
                }
            </dl>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
